09,"implicit"]],"project":false,"range":{"column":0,"endColumn":52,"endLine":43,"line":33},"type":250,"typeText":"{R : Type u_5} →\n  {S : Type u_6} →\n    [inst : Semiring.{u_5} R] →\n      [inst_1 : Semiring.{u_6} S] →\n        [inst_2 : PartialOrder.{u_6} S] →\n          {motive : AbsoluteValue.{u_5, u_6} R S → Sort u} →\n            (t : AbsoluteValue.{u_5, u_6} R S) →\n              ((toMulHom : MulHom.{u_5, u_6} R S) →\n                  (nonneg' : ∀ (x : R), LE.le.{u_6} 0 (MulHom.toFun.{u_5, u_6} toMulHom x)) →\n                    (eq_zero' :\n                        ∀ (x : R), Iff (Eq.{u_6 + 1} (MulHom.toFun.{u_5, u_6} toMulHom x) 0) (Eq.{u_5 + 1} x 0)) →\n                      (add_le' :\n                          ∀ (x y : R),\n                            LE.le.{u_6} (MulHom.toFun.{u_5, u_6} toMulHom (HAdd.hAdd.{u_5, u_5, u_5} x y))\n                              (HAdd.hAdd.{u_6, u_6, u_6} (MulHom.toFun.{u_5, u_6} toMulHom x)\n                                (MulHom.toFun.{u_5, u_6} toMulHom y))) →\n                        motive (AbsoluteValue.mk.{u_5, u_6} toMulHom nonneg' eq_zero' add_le')) →\n                motive t","unsafe":false,"value":410,"source":{"code":"/-- `AbsoluteValue R S` is the type of absolute values on `R` mapping to `S`:\nthe maps that preserve `*`, are nonnegative, positive definite and satisfy\nthe triangle inequality. -/\nstructure AbsoluteValue (R S : Type*) [Semiring R] [Semiring S] [PartialOrder S]\n    extends R →ₙ* S where\n  /-- The absolute value is nonnegative -/\n  nonneg' : ∀ x, 0 ≤ toFun x\n  /-- The absolute value is positive definitive -/\n  eq_zero' : ∀ x, toFun x = 0 ↔ x = 0\n  /-- The absolute value satisfies the triangle inequality -/\n  add_le' : ∀ x y, toFun (x + y) ≤ toFun x + toFun y","start":33,"end":43},"axioms":[]}